- The plan does not explicitly reuse the richer current-state evidence in [docs/document-intelligence/intelligence-accessibility-map.md](/mnt/local-analysis/workspace-hub/docs/document-intelligence/intelligence-accessibility-map.md), which already contains weekly checklist implications and discoverability context relevant to freshness signaling.

8. **Low findings**  
- The plan’s “Standards: N/A” section is acceptable, but it would be stronger to name the repo governance docs it is relying on instead of treating standards as absent.  
- The review artifact path points to a single subagent result, which weakens auditability even aside from the missing second provider.  
- The plan does not state whether [docs/dashboards/doc-freshness-dashboard.md](/mnt/local-analysis/workspace-hub/docs/dashboards/doc-freshness-dashboard.md) remains document-only or becomes a mixed-asset dashboard.

9. **Required revisions before user approval**  
- Reconcile approval state across the issue label, plan file status, and [docs/plans/README.md](/mnt/local-analysis/workspace-hub/docs/plans/README.md). The plan must not appear approved before the actual approval gate is complete.  
- Add the missing adversarial review provider(s) and record them in the plan artifact.  
- Expand retrieval to explicitly cite and use the parent operating model (#2205), the relevant sibling contracts/boundaries, and the already-landed accessibility/freshness surfaces as governing inputs.  
- Make source-of-truth precedence explicit: define whether the matrix is authoritative and how [data/document-index/intelligence-accessibility-registry.yaml](/mnt/local-analysis/workspace-hub/data/document-index/intelligence-accessibility-registry.yaml), weekly review docs, and any scanner/dashboard surfaces consume it.  
- Replace the vague scanner integration step with a concrete implementation decision: either extend current tooling beyond `docs/**/*.md`, add a separate asset-freshness path, or explicitly keep doc-freshness tooling out of scope and document the boundary.  
- Tighten acceptance criteria and verification so they prove all issue deliverables: cadence matrix by asset class, alert levels, freshness evidence sources, automatic vs manual refresh handling, and weekly finding presentation.
